  "notes": "Used in everyday language for light reflecting, and in science for reflection of waves. The noun form {反射|はんしゃ} is also used for involuntary bodily reactions (reflexes).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {反射|はんしゃ}{的|てき}に: reflexively, instinctively\n- {反射|はんしゃ}{神経|しんけい}: reflexes\n- {乱反射|らんはんしゃ}: diffuse reflection\n- {全反射|ぜんはんしゃ}: total reflection\n- {条件|じょうけん}{反射|はんしゃ}: conditioned reflex\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {映|うつ}る: to be reflected, to appear — used for images reflected in mirrors or water\n- {反射|はんしゃ}する: to reflect — used for light, sound, or heat bouncing off surfaces\n- {跳|は}ね{返|かえ}る: to bounce back — physical bouncing of objects",
